    "lastCommit": {
      "id": "a5ea7537175cf5c67aa7136d7219797168faa005",
      "message": "[ota-hal] OTA-1727 \u2014 the card stops cutting the warning off\n\nThree fixed rows, as asked. But I measured the overflow before moving anything,\nand it was worse than a layout complaint.\n\n\u26a0\u26a0\u26a0 THERE WERE TWO SILENT CLIPPING SITES, not one. Neither showed an ellipsis,\nneither scrolled. The text simply was not there.\n\n  ROW 1 was a `flexDirection: 'row'` with NO `flexWrap`. React Native defaults a\n  row to `nowrap`, so every chip past the right edge was cut. Measured on a 320pt\n  row (a 360dp phone less the screen, body and stripe insets):\n\n      plain \u2014 rarity \u00b7 dice \u00b7 durability \u00b7 equip text ...... 185 of 301 weapons\n      coated and reserved ................................. 301 of 301 weapons\n\n  Worst case, the Shockwave Club: 402pt bare, 488pt dressed, into 320.\n\n  ROW 3 was `numberOfLines={1}` \u2014 138 of 301 weapons truncated. What it cut:\n\n      15 weapons never showed that they CANNOT BE COATED\n       3 never showed a PERMANENT armour/shield unlock\n       3 never showed a flat on-hit rider\n       2 never showed the FRIENDLY-FIRE line\n       1 never showed that it eventually EXPLODES in your hands\n       1 never showed that it pierces armour\n\n\u26a0\u26a0 THE FRIENDLY-FIRE ONE IS THE SHARPEST. OTA-1565 added that line with a note\nsaying this card \"is the only warning a player gets before they buy a weapon that\ncan kill their own dog.\" Then Row 3 cut it off. The Ember Storm Stave carries\nfour lines of rules and displayed one:\n\n    Scales with INT \u00b7 On hit: 1d4 burn/turn for 2 turns \u00b7 2d8 to eve\u2026\n\nEverything after that \u2014 the splash, and \"Power weapon \u2014 takes no coating\" \u2014 was\nnever on screen.\n\nTHE THREE ROWS:\n\n  1  rarity \u00b7 damage roll (damage type) \u00b7 durability \u00b7 on-hit / proc\n  2  One-handed | Two-handed \u00b7 tap to equip / EQUIPPED (main hand)\n  3  Scales with STR \u00b7 resistances \u00b7 every special property, in full\n\n\u26a0 FIXED AS LAYOUT, NOT AS TYPE SIZE. You ruled that out by name and the suite\npins it: rowMeta 10, rowHold 10, rowEquippable 10, rowEquipped 10, rowStat 11 \u2014\nfive assertions, so nothing can be quietly shrunk to buy width later. Moving the\nhand and equip chips down to Row 2 is what gives Row 1 its budget back; wrapping\nis what guarantees it can never silently cut again. Measured after:\n\n      Row 1 plain ............ 185 of 301 \u2192 0 of 301 over one line\n      Row 1 coated+reserved .. 301 of 301 \u2192 5 of 301, and those five WRAP\n\n\u26a0 \"HAND\" IS GONE, AND IT WAS THE ODD HALF OF A PAIR. A two-hander announced its\nhand COUNT and a one-hander announced only that it went in a hand \u2014 two answers\nto different questions, so you had to know that \"Hand\" meant \"not the other one\".\nBoth say the count now.\n\n\u26a0 AND THE HAND LABEL READS THROUGH `resolveDisplayWeapon`, not `findWeaponByName`\n\u2014 the OTA-705 rule. A fused piece is catalog-absent by design and its name can\ncollide with an unrelated catalog row, so the name lookup could read a\ntwo-hander's style off a fused vest that merely shares its name. Same defect\nOTA-705 fixed for the damage dice, one field over.\n\n\u26a0 ROW 3 HOISTS THE SCALING STAT. It already led for most weapons, but only by the\naccident of `previewWeapon` pushing `Scales with` second and the row filtering out\nthe first entry. Row order is your requirement, so it belongs to the row.\n\n\u26a0 AND A GATE CAUGHT ME WRITING THE BUG I SPENT TODAY FIXING. My first\n\"numberOfLines is gone\" assertion used a fixed 120-BYTE window, and\n`check:slicepins` refused it: a negative pin measured in bytes goes SILENT as soon\nas code grows between the anchor and the forbidden text \u2014 it stops checking at\nexactly the moment it should scream. Rewritten on `between` + `expectAbsent`,\nwhich bounds the window by the code's own shape and carries a canary proving the\nwindow still looks at the right element.\n\n12 tests, on a REAL render of the screen \u2014 the section defaults collapsed, so the\nsuite expands it and self-checks that the rows are actually there before\nasserting anything about them. 19 gates green, complete surface clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
      "dateCreated": "2026-09-07T01:09:17Z",
